            <ArticleTitle>Imperfect crowding adaptation of mammalian cells towards osmotic stress and its modulation by osmolytes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2218-2221</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7mb00432j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Changes of the extracellular milieu could affect cellular crowding. To prevent detrimental effects, cells use adaptation mechanisms to react to such conditions. Using fluorescent crowding sensors, we show that the initial response to osmotic stress is fast but imperfect, while the slow response renders cells more tolerant to stress, particularly in the presence of osmolytes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
